So the function trims a trailing `\n` and then a trailing `\r` (in that order), i.e. handles CRLF line endings.

## Notable Data References
- `0x286dd0` / `0x286dd8`: `main::get_path::__STATIC_FMTSTR` (format string pieces).
- `0x670d0`: `str.t` — likely the prompt text (also used as the panic message for `expect` at `0x1fe01`, length `0x1e` = 30 bytes).

